From e37fb938b50c0a511525fe57a894fb32b5f6dc4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TickTrade Workbench <hmodebdwie1@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 21:27:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(creator): port TickTrade Studio onto the round-12
 backend

Round 12 contains no Creator Platform code, so this is the same port previously
made onto round 9, re-applied to the newer line. The three seam files
(app.module.ts, apps/api/package.json, packages/shared/prisma/schema.prisma) are
byte-identical between round 9 and round 12, so the port applies verbatim; none
of round 12's 19 changed or 5 new files touch it.

New: apps/api/src/creator/ (24), packages/tickscript/ (14), and 4 Prisma
migrations. Seam: import and register CreatorModule, add the
@ticktrade/tickscript workspace dependency, and append 17 Creator* models plus
2 User relation fields to schema.prisma with its existing CRLF endings.

Carries the fixes made on the round-9 port:
- the two quadratic hot spots in the DataBank build (21x at 640k events,
  byte-identical output),
- percentile ranking rebuilt once per bank instead of per record,
- every unavailable DataBank field now states why it is unavailable,
- a CPU-aware supervisor deadline so a starved script is not killed while a
  runaway one still is,
- DELETE /creator/scripts/:id, so the 50-script private library limit is
  recoverable; it refuses while a tool is still attached and never destroys a
  live expert journal.

Verified on round 12: prisma migrate deploy with zero schema drift, clean api
build, tickscript 25/25, api jest 58 suites / 335 tests, and live acceptance
against a running stack (lifecycle 13/13, DataBank 8/8, paper expert 10/10).
